has been with Tucker Carlson at Fox News.&nbsp;
Part of it's restricting access. Then also,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:19:38.100 --> 00:19:42.780
demonizing the media on social media. He's very&nbsp;
aggressive through Twitter, where he's just&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:19:42.780 --> 00:19:47.160
constantly attacking journalists to the point of&nbsp;
calling journalists "gang members" and harassing&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:19:47.160 --> 00:19:51.840
them and scaring them out of the country. But&nbsp;
that's where people are getting their news. One&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:19:51.840 --> 00:19:56.760
thing that's interesting here in El Salvador, for&nbsp;
instance, is the majority of people rely on news&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:19:56.760 --> 00:20:01.560
that comes from government-run media because&nbsp;
those are the only media that's reaching rural&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:20:01.560 --> 00:20:06.000
communities or people that don't have access.&nbsp;
So, the only thing they're hearing is what the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:20:06.000 --> 00:20:10.200
government is telling them that they should&nbsp;
be believing, and then constantly demonizing&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:20:10.200 --> 00:20:13.800
the opposition or anyone that speaks out or&nbsp;
says anything different than the party line.
&nbsp;

00:20:13.800 --> 00:20:20.220
SIERRA: But aside from Bukele’s influencer&nbsp;
status, he has also achieved a feat many thought&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:20:20.220 --> 00:20:28.200
impossible. In March of 2022, Bukele officially&nbsp;
